# CLAUDE.md

**Read [AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md) before planning, coding, or answering.**
This file contains no project instructions of its own — it exists only
because **Claude Code** reads `CLAUDE.md` by default.

`AGENTS.md` is the canonical source of code conventions for this repository.
The ASDD workflow (Spec → Scan → Plan → Ticket → Build → PR) lives in
`asdd/ai-workflow/`:

- Read `asdd/ai-workflow/ASDD.md` for the master flow and phase definitions.
- For each phase load `asdd/ai-workflow/skills/<name>.md` (base) plus the profile
  overlay `asdd/ai-workflow/skills/<name>.<profile>.md`, where `<profile>` is
  `fe` or `be` and is read from the `asdd_profile:` frontmatter in
  `AGENTS.md` (or from `asdd/config.yml`).
- Apply the self-verification loop from
  `asdd/ai-workflow/prompts/loop-self-verify.md` on every artifact.
- Follow the token-efficiency and minimal-comments rules from
  [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md) (Rules #6 and #7). No inline comments in
  generated code except when genuinely necessary; no preambles or closing
  summaries in responses.
- **Bootstrap trigger.** If the user says `Start ASDD`, `Iniciar ASDD`,
  `Run ASDD`, or `asdd init` (case-insensitive), load
  `asdd/ai-workflow/prompts/bootstrap.md` first and follow it.
